/Title (The strategy is sound. The capital is in place. The board has approved direction. And yet the organisation cannot move. Decisions take too long to translate into action. Targets are missed for reasons no one can fully explain. Costs rise faster than output. Good people leave. Less good people stay. Critical roles sit unfilled for months. Performance reviews produce paperwork but not behaviour change. The same problems surface in the same management meetings, quarter after quarter.)
